  const UD = {"reachBy":["Every pick-up moves later by the same amount. Routes do not change.","Every pick-up moves earlier. Routes that would start before Earliest Pick-up are split, which can add buses."],"earliest":["Less time before school, so long routes are split. Expect more buses and shorter rides.","Routes may start earlier and run longer, so fewer buses. Some students are picked up earlier."],"arrFrom":["The window narrows from the front. More buses arrive close together at the gate.","The window widens. Buses can arrive earlier and are spread out more at the gate."],"arrTo":["The window widens. Late buses can arrive later instead of starting earlier.","The window narrows. Late buses start their pick-ups earlier."],"targetCap":["Routes may run longer before paying points. Fewer, fuller buses and longer rides.","Over Target points start sooner. More buses and shorter journeys."],"hardCap":["Longer routes are allowed. Fewer buses, but some students ride much longer.","Long routes are split. More buses and no very long rides. Too low can leave far riders unplanned."],"traffic":["Every drive is planned slower. Earlier pick-ups and journeys hit the limits sooner, so more buses.","Drives are planned faster. Later pick-ups and fewer buses, but buses may run late on the day."],"baseDwell":["Each stop costs more time. The engine prefers fewer, bigger stops and routes get shorter in stop count.","Stops cost less. Routes can take more small stops, but pick-up times may be too tight on the day."],"perStudent":["Big stops take longer. Journeys grow and buses fill to fewer students before hitting time limits.","Boarding is planned faster. Tighter times, but buses may fall behind at large stops."],"schoolDwell":["More time at the gate. AM buses start earlier, PM buses leave the gate later.","Less time at the gate. Tighter times at school."],"headroom":["More seats are kept free on every bus. Fewer riders per bus, so more buses.","Buses are planned fuller. Fewer buses, but less room for late joiners."],"overtime":["Going over Target costs more. The engine adds buses to keep journeys near Target.","Going over Target is cheap. Fewer buses with longer journeys, up to Max Journey."],"floorPenalty":["Half-empty buses cost more. The engine merges them or switches to smaller buses.","The engine accepts emptier buses when that gives shorter or simpler routes."],"pointPen":["Moving a family costs more. Plans change less between runs, even if a better plan exists.","Families are moved more freely. Plans change more for smaller gains."],"runs":["More independent searches. A better plan is more likely, but the run takes longer.","Fewer searches. Faster, but the plan may be less good."],"timeLimit":["The engine may search longer. Better plans on big schools, slower results.","The search is cut off sooner. Faster, rougher plans."],"effort":["More runs and more time. Better plans, longer waits.","Fewer runs, less time. Quick what-ifs with rougher plans."],"gapPen":["Long empty drives cost more. Buses stay inside one cluster, even if that adds a bus.","Buses may hop between clusters to fill seats. Fewer buses, more zig-zag."],"gapMin":["Buses in estates may drive further between stops without points. Routes can spread out.","Buses in estates must hop short distances. Tighter routes, maybe more buses."],"gapMax":["In spread-out areas, buses may drive further between stops. Fewer buses for remote riders.","Remote riders are harder to combine. They may get their own bus."],"maxSectorDeg":["Each bus may cover a wider slice around school. Fuller buses, more crossing across town.","Each bus stays in a narrower direction. Cleaner routes, but more half-empty buses."],"sectorFromKm":["More stops near school ignore the direction rule, so they can join any bus.","Stops near school must follow the direction rule. Fewer options for them."],"maxDetour":["Students may ride further past home. Fewer buses, longer rides for some.","Rides stay close to the direct drive. More buses, shorter rides."],"detourGrace":["Students near school may ride longer, so they can share buses with farther riders.","Students near school must ride almost direct. They may get their own bus."],"rideCost":["Every minute on board costs more. Shorter rides even if buses drive further or add a bus.","Ride time matters less. Fewer buses and less driving, longer rides."],"loopbackM":["Only big turn-backs are flagged. Fewer warnings.","Small turn-backs are flagged too. More warnings to check."],"rrMax":["Each round reshapes more of the plan. Explores more, slower to settle.","Each round makes small changes. Fine-tunes, may get stuck in a so-so plan."],"ants":["More stop orders tried per bus. Better order, slower.","Fewer orders tried. Faster, order may be less good."],"acoIters":["More rounds per bus. Better order, slower.","Fewer rounds. Faster, order may be less good."],"sweepStarts":["More starting plans tried. Better start, slightly slower.","Fewer starting plans. Faster, the search starts from a weaker plan."]};
  const NEWI = {"detourPen":{"t":"Detour Penalty","what":"Points for every minute a bus goes out of its way for one pick-up, beyond Free Detour.","how":["For each stop, the engine compares the drive previous stop → this stop → next stop with driving previous → next directly.","The extra minutes above Free Detour are charged.","Paired with three-bus exchanges: a full bus can hand a stop on so the bus already passing nearby takes the rider."],"ex":"A pick-up that adds 6 min, 3 min free, 15 pts/min: 3 × 15 = 45 pts.","score":"Makes off-path pick-ups expensive, so the engine reshuffles riders onto the bus already passing them.","tune":"Raise it if buses still leave their path for single riders. 0 turns it off.","up":"Off-path pick-ups cost more. Each bus keeps to its own path. May add a bus when no nearby seats are free.","down":"Detours are cheap again. Fewer buses, but more out-of-the-way pick-ups."},"detourFree":{"t":"Free Detour","what":"Extra minutes one pick-up may add to the path before Detour Penalty applies.","how":["Small detours are normal: turning into a car park or round a block.","Only the minutes above this are charged."],"ex":"At 3 min, a 2 min side trip costs nothing; a 6 min side trip pays for 3 min.","score":"Sets where Detour Penalty starts to bite.","tune":"Lower it in dense estates; raise it in landed areas with one-way roads.","up":"Bigger side trips are free. More detours before any points, fewer buses.","down":"Even small side trips cost points. Tighter paths, more reshuffling."},"areaPen":{"t":"Split Area Penalty","what":"Points each time an area of nearby stops is served by more than one bus.","how":["Stops within Area Size of each other form one area.","A bus carrying only part of an area pays its share. Two buses in one area add up to the full points; three buses, twice.","Areas with more riders than one bus can carry are not penalised."],"ex":"An area of 8 riders split 5 and 3 between two buses: 80 pts in total.","score":"Pushes one bus to collect the whole area before moving on. Can add a bus when buses are full.","tune":"0 = off. Try 80 and compare plans with it off.","up":"Areas are kept on one bus more strictly. Cleaner maps, but may need an extra bus.","down":"Areas can be shared between buses. Fewer buses, more overlap."},"areaM":{"t":"Area Size","what":"Stops within this distance of each other count as one area for Split Area Penalty.","how":["Areas chain: if A is near B and B is near C, all three are one area.","Only used when Split Area Penalty is above 0."],"ex":"At 300 m, two blocks across the road are one area; a block 1 km away is not.","score":"Bigger areas mean more stops the engine tries to keep on one bus.","tune":"Use 200 to 400 m in HDB estates.","up":"Areas get bigger and chain together. More stops must share a bus; large areas become too big and stop counting.","down":"Areas shrink to the closest stops only. Less pull to group, fewer extra buses."}};
  const I = {
    reachBy: { t: 'Reach School By', what: 'The time buses aim to arrive at school (AM). In PM sessions this is Leave School At.', how: ['Every pick-up time is worked backwards from it: drive times, traffic factor and dwell times.', 'Buses are then spread across the Arrival Window.'], ex: 'At 07:45, a stop 23 min away by bus is picked up at about 07:22.', score: 'No points. It sets the clock every other time rule is measured against.', tune: 'Change it when the school bell time changes.' },
    earliest: { t: 'Earliest Pick-up', what: 'No student is picked up before this time.', how: ['A route that would need an earlier first pick-up is not allowed.', 'The engine splits or rearranges it instead.'], ex: 'At 06:45 with arrival at 07:45, no route can be longer than about 60 min.', score: 'A hard rule, not points. A tight limit can add buses.', tune: 'Move it earlier only if families agree to earlier pick-ups.' },
    arrFrom: { t: 'Arrival Window From', what: 'The earliest a bus may arrive at school. In PM sessions, the earliest a bus may leave.', how: ['Buses are spread across the window so the gate is not jammed.', 'A bus planned to arrive earlier starts its pick-ups later.'], ex: 'Window 07:30 to 07:45: a bus planned for 07:25 is moved to 07:30.', score: 'No points. It shifts times, not routes.', tune: 'Widen the window if the drop-off bay is crowded.' },
    arrTo: { t: 'Arrival Window To', what: 'The latest a bus may arrive at school. In PM sessions, the latest a bus may leave.', how: ['A bus planned to arrive later starts its pick-ups earlier.', 'Earlier starts must still respect Earliest Pick-up.'], ex: 'Window 07:30 to 07:45: a bus planned for 07:50 is moved to 07:45.', score: 'No points. It shifts times, not routes.', tune: 'Keep it a few minutes before the school bell.' },
    targetCap: { t: 'Target Journey', what: 'The journey time each route should aim for, from first pick-up to school (AM) or school to last drop-off (PM).', how: ['Routes may run longer.', 'Each minute over adds Over Target Journey points.'], ex: 'Target 50: a 42 min route costs nothing extra, a 56 min route pays for 6 min.', score: 'The engine weighs these points against adding a bus.', tune: 'Lower it for shorter rides; expect more buses.' },
    hardCap: { t: 'Max Journey', what: 'No route may be longer than this, from first pick-up to school.', how: ['A hard wall: routes that would pass it are split or rearranged.', 'Should be above Target Journey.'], ex: 'Max 75: an 80 min route is split onto two buses.', score: 'A hard rule, not points. Never traded for a lower score.', tune: 'Set it to the longest ride families will accept.' },
    traffic: { t: 'Peak Traffic Factor', what: 'Road times come from the map with no traffic. This factor stretches every driving time to match the hour the buses run.', how: ['Every leg between stops and to school is multiplied by it.', 'Dwell time at stops is not affected.', 'Each session has its own factor (AM, PM, ASA/CCA).'], ex: 'A leg that takes 20 min on empty roads is planned as 28 min at 1.4.', score: 'Longer times raise running points and make Target and Max Journey easier to break, so the engine may need more buses.', tune: 'Raise it if buses arrive late in real life; lower it if they are early.' },
    baseDwell: { t: 'Dwell Time | Per Stop', what: 'Fixed time lost at every stop: slowing down, pulling in, opening the door, closing it and rejoining traffic.', how: ['Added once per stop, no matter how many students board.', 'Counts towards the journey time and pick-up times.'], ex: 'A route with 10 stops loses 10 × 30 s = 5 min to stopping alone.', score: 'Each extra stop makes a route longer, so the engine prefers fewer, fuller stops.', tune: 'Raise it for busy roads or tight kerbs.' },
    perStudent: { t: 'Dwell Time | Per Student', what: 'Extra time for each student to get on or off: walking up, finding a seat, fastening a belt.', how: ['Added for every student at the stop, on top of Per Stop.'], ex: '4 students at one stop: 30 s + 4 × 5 s = 50 s.', score: 'Large stops take longer, which shows up in journey time and ride points.', tune: 'Raise it for younger students.' },
    schoolDwell: { t: 'Dwell Time | At School', what: 'Time at the school gate to unload everyone in the morning, or load everyone in the afternoon.', how: ['Added once per route at the school end.', 'Not counted as ride time for students who have already got off.'], ex: 'At 2 min, a PM bus leaving at 13:45 starts driving at 13:47.', score: 'Affects timings more than points.', tune: 'Raise it if the bay is crowded.' },
    headroom: { t: 'Headroom', what: 'Seats kept free on each bus type so late joiners can be added without re-planning.', how: ['Loads up to = student seats × (1 − headroom), rounded down.', 'Hard Limit Yes: the engine never fills those seats.', 'Hard Limit No: it may fill them when that saves a whole bus.'], ex: '23-seater, 10%: planned to 20 riders, 3 seats spare.', score: 'More headroom means fewer riders per bus, so more buses and more Bus Use points.', tune: 'Use 0% for a fixed list that will not change.' },
    overtime: { t: 'Over Target Journey', what: 'Points for each minute a route runs past Target Journey.', how: ['Journey is first pick-up to school (AM), or school to last drop-off (PM).', 'Under Target costs nothing extra.', 'Max Journey is a hard wall: no route may pass it at all.'], ex: 'Target 50, route 55 min, 15 pts/min: 5 × 15 = 75 pts.', score: 'Compared with Bus Use points: if splitting a route into two buses costs less than its overtime points, the engine splits it.', tune: 'Raise it to keep journeys shorter even if it adds buses.' },
    floorPenalty: { t: 'Below Min Fill', what: 'Points for every rider a bus is short of its Min Fill, set per bus type.', how: ['Min Fill is a % of student seats.', 'Only buses below it get points.'], ex: '23-seater, Min Fill 13, carrying 8: 5 short × 10 pts = 50 pts.', score: 'Pushes the engine to merge near-empty buses or switch to a smaller bus.', tune: 'Raise it if you see many half-empty buses.' },
    pointPen: { t: 'Point Change', what: 'Points for moving a rider to a different pick-up point than in the current plan.', how: ['Only used when Stability is Keep Current.', 'Charged per rider moved.', 'Pick-up times that shift more than a few minutes are also counted.'], ex: 'Moving a family of 2 to another point: 2 × 3 = 6 pts.', score: 'A move only happens if it saves more points than it costs, so families are not moved for tiny gains.', tune: 'Raise it mid-term to keep changes to a minimum.' },
    runs: { t: 'Runs', what: 'How many full searches the engine does, each from a different random start.', how: ['Each run builds a plan and improves it independently.', 'The plan with the lowest total score is kept.', 'The time limit is shared fairly across runs.'], ex: '3 runs scoring 9,420, 9,119 and 9,610 pts: the 9,119 plan is kept.', score: 'More runs make a lower score more likely; they do not change how points are counted.', tune: '3 is a good balance. Use 5 to 10 for the final plan of the term.' },
    timeLimit: { t: 'Time Limit', what: 'A safety cut-off for the whole search, 60 seconds at most.', how: ['Normally the runs finish on their own counts first.', 'If the server is busy or the school is large, the clock stops the search.', 'The best plan found so far is always kept.'], ex: '3 runs, 60 s: each run gets about 20 s.', score: 'Does not change the score, only how long the engine may look for a lower one.', tune: 'Leave at 60 unless you want quicker, rougher plans.' },
    effort: { t: 'Effort', what: 'How hard the engine searches for a better plan. Higher effort tries more runs and is allowed more time.', how: ['Low: 1 run, up to 15 s. Med: 2 runs, 30 s. High: 3 runs, 60 s. Extra: 5 runs, 90 s. Max: 8 runs, 120 s.', 'Each run starts from a different random choice. The lowest score is kept.', 'Each run stops early once it stops finding improvements, so plans often finish sooner.'], ex: 'High on a 400-rider school: 3 runs, usually done in 20 to 40 s.', score: 'Does not change how points are counted, only how likely a lower total is found.', tune: 'Med for quick what-ifs, High day to day, Extra or Max for the final plan of the term. The levels available depend on the Convoy plan.' },
    gapPen: { t: 'Cluster Focus', what: 'Keeps each bus inside one cluster of riders before heading to school, instead of picking a few, driving far, then picking more.', how: ['Every drive between two pick-ups is compared with an allowed empty leg.', 'Each minute over the allowance adds points.', 'The allowance depends on how many riders live nearby (see Dense and Sparse Area).'], ex: 'An 11 min leg in a dense area (4 min allowed): 7 × 12 = 84 pts.', score: 'Usually cheaper to reshuffle stops between buses than to pay these points, so buses stay local.', tune: 'Raise to 20+ to force tighter clusters. 0 turns it off.' },
    gapMin: { t: 'Empty Leg | Dense Area', what: 'The longest drive allowed between two pick-ups where many riders live close together.', how: ['Dense means 30 or more riders within 1.5 km of the stop.', 'Between dense and sparse the allowance scales smoothly.'], ex: 'At 4 min, a bus in a busy estate should reach its next stop within 4 min.', score: 'Minutes over it are charged at the Cluster Focus rate.', tune: 'Lower it to keep buses tighter in estates.' },
    gapMax: { t: 'Empty Leg | Sparse Area', what: 'The longest drive allowed between two pick-ups where riders are spread out.', how: ['Used for stops with few riders around them.', 'A longer allowance lets one bus cover a wide, thin area.'], ex: 'At 12 min, a bus may drive up to 12 min between landed-house stops.', score: 'Minutes over it are charged at the Cluster Focus rate.', tune: 'Raise it if remote riders get their own bus too often.' },
    maxSectorDeg: { t: 'Max Sector Width', what: 'Keeps each bus to one direction from school, like one slice of a clock face, so it does not zig-zag across town.', how: ['Measured as the angle between a route\'s stops, seen from the school.', 'Set for stops about 10 km away. Routes nearer school may spread up to 3× wider, because stops that look far apart in angle are a short drive apart.', 'Stops within Sector Ignores Within are left out.'], ex: 'At 40°, stops spread over 120° at 10 km are split onto separate buses.', score: 'A hard rule, not points. A route that breaks it is never used.', tune: 'Raise it if buses look half-empty in outer areas; 0 turns it off.' },
    sectorFromKm: { t: 'Sector Ignores Within', what: 'Stops this close to school are left out of the Max Sector Width check.', how: ['Near the gate every direction meets, so angle means little.', 'Stops inside still count for time, seats and every other rule.'], ex: 'At 2 km, a stop 1 km north can join a route heading east.', score: 'A hard rule, not points.', tune: 'Raise it for a school in a dense town centre.' },
    maxDetour: { t: 'Max Ride Detour', what: 'The longest a student may ride compared with driving straight from their stop to school.', how: ['Allowed ride = direct drive × this factor + Detour Grace.', 'A route that breaks it for any student is refused.'], ex: 'Direct 10 min, factor 2.5, grace 10: up to 35 min on board.', score: 'A hard rule, not points. Student Ride Time handles the softer pressure.', tune: 'Lower it to stop long ride-arounds; 0 turns it off.' },
    detourGrace: { t: 'Detour Grace', what: 'Extra minutes added on top of Max Ride Detour.', how: ['Protects students living near school, whose direct drive is very short.'], ex: 'Direct 4 min × 2.5 = 10 min, plus 10 grace = 20 min allowed.', score: 'A hard rule, not points.', tune: 'Raise it if near-school students keep getting their own bus.' },
    rideCost: { t: 'Student Ride Time', what: 'Points for every minute each student spends on board.', how: ['Counted per student, from boarding to arrival.', 'A small number on purpose: it breaks ties between similar plans.'], ex: '3 students riding 30, 20 and 10 min = 60 rider-minutes × 0.02 = 1.2 pts.', score: 'Makes the engine prefer orders where most students board late and ride less.', tune: 'Raise it to cut long rides, even if buses drive further.' },
    loopbackM: { t: 'Loop-back Threshold', what: 'Flags a route when the bus heads back away from school by more than this distance.', how: ['A warning badge only. The route is still allowed.'], ex: 'At 500 m, a bus that turns 800 m back away from school is flagged.', score: 'No points.', tune: '0 turns the warning off.' },
    rrMax: { t: 'Max Stops Removed', what: 'Ruin & Recreate takes a few stops out of the plan and puts each back in its best place.', how: ['Stops are picked as a nearby group, at random, the worst-placed ones, or a whole route.', 'The new plan is kept if its score is better, or sometimes slightly worse early on to escape dead ends.'], ex: 'At 12, each round moves up to 12 stops.', score: 'Explores more plans, each judged by the same points.', tune: 'Higher explores more, lower fine-tunes.' },
    ants: { t: 'Ants per Iteration', what: 'Tunes the order of stops inside each bus using Ant Colony Optimisation.', how: ['Each ant builds one stop order.', 'Short, good orders leave a stronger trail for the next round.'], ex: '14 ants try 14 orders per round.', score: 'Better orders lower running and ride points.', tune: 'More ants find better orders but take longer.' },
    acoIters: { t: 'ACO Iterations', what: 'How many rounds the ants run for each bus.', how: ['Each round strengthens the best order found so far.'], ex: '100 rounds × 14 ants = 1,400 orders tried per bus.', score: 'Better orders lower running and ride points.', tune: 'Raise it for the final plan; lower it for quick tries.' },
    sweepStarts: { t: 'Sweep Start Angles', what: 'Builds the first plan by sweeping around the school like a clock hand, filling buses as it goes.', how: ['Several start angles are tried, clockwise and anti-clockwise.', 'The cheapest grouping becomes the starting plan.'], ex: 'At 8, 16 sweeps are tried.', score: 'A better start lets the search reach a lower score sooner.', tune: 'Raise it for large schools.' },
    scoring: { t: 'How Scoring Works', what: 'Every plan gets a score in points. The engine tries thousands of plans and keeps the lowest total.', how: ['Bus Use: each bus adds its Use Penalty (set per bus type).', 'Running: 1 pt per bus-minute of journey.', 'Over Target Journey, Below Min Fill, Student Ride Time, Cluster Focus, Detour Penalty, Split Area Penalty and Point Change add their own points.', 'Hard rules are never traded for points: Max Journey, seats, Max Sector Width and Max Ride Detour must always hold.'], ex: 'Plan A: 3 buses, one 5 min over target = 390 pts.\nPlan B: 2 buses, all on time = 280 pts. Plan B wins.', score: 'Raising a penalty makes that problem more expensive, so the engine trades other things to avoid it.', tune: 'Priority presets set these for you. Change one at a time and compare plans.' }
  };
  Object.keys(UD).forEach(k => { if (I[k]) { I[k].up = UD[k][0]; I[k].down = UD[k][1]; } }); Object.assign(I, NEWI, {
    accRenew: { t: 'Auto-Accept Renewing Riders', what: 'Current riders who apply in the renewal window keep their seat without waiting for you.', how: ["Applies to riders on this year's list who apply between Renewals From and Renewals To.", 'The three checks under it can send some renewals to you instead.', 'The parent still confirms within the confirm time, or the offer lapses.'], ex: 'Aisha rides AM and PM this year and renews with the same address. Accepted on submit.', tune: 'Leave on unless every renewal needs a look, for example after a big route change.' },
    accAddr: { t: 'Send to Me if the Home Address Changed', what: 'A renewal with a new home address waits for you instead of being accepted.', how: ["The postal code is compared with this year's rider record.", 'A new address may need a different stop or bus.'], ex: 'Ben moved from Jurong West to Tampines. His renewal waits so you can check the stop.', tune: 'Turn off only if you will move riders to new stops during routing anyway.' },
    accSes: { t: 'Send to Me if a Session Is Added', what: 'A renewal that adds a session the rider does not ride today waits for you.', how: ['Dropping a session is still accepted.', 'Adding one needs a seat on a bus the rider is not on yet.'], ex: 'Hana rides AM only this year and applies for AM and PM. Her renewal waits.', tune: 'Leave on when PM or CCA buses are close to full.' },
    accDebt: { t: 'Send to Me if the Family Has Overdue Bills', what: 'A renewal from a family with an unpaid bill past its due date waits for you.', how: ['Bills not yet due do not count.', 'You decide whether to accept, waitlist or follow up on payment first.'], ex: "Dan's June bill is 21 days overdue. His renewal waits.", tune: 'Turn off if overdue bills are handled separately by finance.' },
    accNear: { t: 'Auto-Accept New Applicants Near School', what: 'Families with no current rider are accepted when their home is close to school.', how: ['Distance is a straight line from school to home.', 'Set the distance in Home Within.', 'Add the seat check to accept only where a bus has room.'], ex: 'Home Within 3 km. A home 2.1 km away is accepted. One 4.8 km away waits for you.', tune: 'Use for schools that must serve nearby families first.' },
    seatCheck: { t: "Seat Check on This Year's Routes", what: 'Accepts only when a stop covers the address and its bus has a free seat.', how: ["Next year is not routed yet, so the check uses this year's AM plan.", 'Seats of riders who are leaving count as free. Offers waiting for a parent to confirm hold their seat.', 'A seat must be left after Seats Kept Free per Bus. The spare seats allow for next year\'s routes changing.'], ex: 'Its bus has 20 seats: 3 are empty and 2 riders are leaving, so 5 are free. After keeping 3 free, 2 are left, so the applicant is accepted.', tune: 'Leave on. Without it, applicants may be accepted where no bus can take them.' },
    accSib: { t: 'Auto-Accept Siblings of Current Riders', what: 'A new child whose parent already has a rider this year is accepted.', how: ['Matched on the family group ID. Children in the same family account share it.', 'Phone numbers are not used, since they can change.', 'Add the seat check to accept only where a bus has room.'], ex: "Sam is applied for under Aisha's family group, FID20418. Sam is accepted.", tune: 'Use when the school keeps siblings on the same bus.' },
    accRun: { t: 'Run Auto-Accept', what: 'Choose when the rules run.', how: ['As They Arrive: each application is checked the moment it is submitted.', 'Once a Day: everything since the last run is checked together at the time set in At.'], ex: 'Once a Day at 09:00. Applications from Monday evening are accepted at 09:00 on Tuesday.', tune: 'Use Once a Day to look over new applications each morning before seats are given.' },
    accBuf: { t: 'Seats Kept Free per Bus', what: 'Auto-accept stops when a bus is down to this many free seats.', how: ['Kept-free seats are yours to give from Bus Applications.', "They also allow for next year's routes changing."], ex: 'A 20-seater has 15 riders, so 5 seats are free. With 3 kept free, the next 2 applicants are accepted. The 3rd waits for you, and you can give it a kept-free seat.', tune: "Keep it higher before routing. Lower it once next year's routes are set." },
    accWl: { t: 'Offer Freed Seats to the Waitlist Automatically', what: 'When a seat frees up, the next waitlisted family on that stop gets the offer.', how: ['Renewing families go first, then by submission time.', 'The parent confirms within the confirm time set above.'], ex: 'A rider on Stop 12 withdraws. Elle is renewing and first on the Stop 12 waitlist, so she gets the offer.', tune: 'Turn on once registration is busy and you do not want to watch for withdrawals.' }
  });
  I.accIntro = { t: 'What Auto-Accept Does', what: 'Auto-accept decides some applications for you, so you only review the ones that need a look.', how: ['Each application is checked against the rules you turn on below.', 'A match is accepted and the parent is asked to confirm.', 'No match, or flagged by a check: it waits for you in Bus Applications.', 'Nothing is ever rejected automatically.'], ex: '150 applications come in: 120 renewals and 30 new families. 100 renewals are accepted on submit. You review the other 50.', tune: 'Turn on the rules for decisions you would make the same way every time.' };
  const ACC_UD = {
    accIntro: ['Matching applications are decided as they come in. Parents hear back sooner.', 'Every application waits for you in Bus Applications.', 'Fewer applications to review by hand. Every auto-accepted one still shows in Bus Applications.'],
    accRenew: ['Renewals are accepted as they arrive, unless a check under it sends them to you.', 'Every renewal waits for you, even riders with no changes.', "Usually most of next year's riders. Turning it off adds them all to your review list."],
    accAddr: ['Renewals with a new postal code wait for you.', 'Renewals are accepted at the new address, even if no stop covers it yet.', 'On is safer when buses are close to full or the new home is far from any stop.'],
    accSes: ['Renewals that add AM, PM or CCA wait for you.', 'Added sessions are accepted with no seat check.', 'Off can fill PM and CCA buses past their seats before routing.'],
    accDebt: ['Renewals from families with overdue bills wait for you.', 'Overdue bills do not affect renewals.', 'On gives you a chance to follow up on payment before the seat is confirmed.'],
    accNear: ['New families within Home Within are accepted.', 'Every new family waits for you.', 'A larger distance accepts more families and fills seats faster.'],
    seatCheck: ["Accepted only when a stop covers the home and its bus has a seat on this year's routes.", 'Accepted on distance or sibling match alone, even with no stop or seat.', 'Off can over-fill buses or accept homes no stop covers. Those families may need a new stop after routing.'],
    accSib: ['Children in the same family group as a current rider are accepted.', 'Siblings wait for you like any new family.', 'Keeps families together, but can take seats nearer families were waiting for.'],
    accRun: ['Parents hear back within minutes of applying.', 'Applications wait until the set time. You can review them first.', 'Same rules either way. Once a Day gives you time to step in before seats go.'],
    accBuf: ['Auto-accept stops sooner. More seats are left for you to give by hand.', 'More applications are accepted automatically. Less room for route changes.', 'Set too low before routing, buses may be full once next year is routed.'],
    accWl: ['Freed seats go to the next waitlisted family on that stop straight away.', 'Freed seats stay empty until you offer them from Bus Applications.', 'On fills seats faster. Off lets you choose who gets each seat.']
  };
  Object.keys(ACC_UD).forEach(k => { const v = ACC_UD[k]; Object.assign(I[k], { up: v[0], down: v[1], score: v[2] }); });
